From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 the sites behind a tab's blocked count (ABI 1.69)

Engine side of "Blocked on this page" (docs/FEATURE-SPECS/CONTENT-BLOCKING.md,
section 3). The owner: "How do we see the blocked trackers?" The site
controls row said "N blocked on this page" and the engine had only N:
ActionTracker's per-tab action count for "ReArc Blocker" (tab/095).

Where the sites are kept. ActionTracker::OnRuleMatched is the one place that
knows a blocked request's address, its tab and the ruleset whose rule
matched. At the two lines where it increments the tab's action count
(TrackedInfo::action_count, and the pending count of a main frame
navigation's own request) it now also records the request's site and the
ruleset ID in the same TrackedInfo (TrackedInfo::blocked), for the built-in
blocker only. A member of TrackedInfo has the count's lifetime without a
line of its own:

- a main frame navigation that commits to another document replaces the
  tab's TrackedInfo, with what blocked that navigation's own request or with
  an empty one (ResetTrackedInfoForTab);
- a closed tab's is erased (ClearTabData), an unloaded blocker's too
  (ClearExtensionData);
- a same-document navigation resets nothing, as for the count.

The alternative, callbacks through ExtensionsAPIClient into a map in the
bridge, needs three hooks (match, reset with the navigation ID, abandoned
navigation) and a second lifetime that can drift from the count.

What is kept (security/PRE-blocked-list.md, BL-01, BL-02, BL-05, BL-06):

- The registrable domain of the request's host, private registries included
  ("someone.github.io" stays itself); an IP address as it is; a host with no
  registrable domain (a single label, a public suffix such as "co.uk") as it
  is, marked as not one site, so the host never offers to allow it. No
  address, path, query, resource type or time.
- Only where the action count is incremented: never for a request without a
  tab, so nothing is kept under the unknown tab ID, which nothing resets.
  TransferRulesOnTabInvalid moves matched rules to that ID and is not
  changed: it leaves the sites where they are.
- Only for the two blocker IDs, compiled into action_tracker.cc
  (KeepsBlockedSites). //extensions cannot include the bridge's header, so
  the IDs are written there a second time, as allowlist.cc does;
  engine/tests/check_blocked_hosts_patch.py holds them to
  rearc::kContentBlockerExtensionIds. No call, preference or switch adds an
  ID; every other extension's TrackedInfo is as upstream.
- At most 100 sites per blocker and tab, a name of at most 253 bytes, at most
  8 rulesets a site; a count stops at its largest value; a blocked request
  past a limit is counted in "more".
- Memory only. Nothing is logged. getMatchedRules, onRuleMatchedDebug and
  every other extension API are untouched; the blocker's manifest is
  untouched (one permission, no host access, security CB-03).

The call. ReArcTabCopyBlockedHosts(tab_id, &json) reads ActionTracker for
both blocker IDs with the tab ID ExtensionActionRunner resets and clears it
with (ExtensionTabUtil::GetTabId), adds a site's entries up while a list
update has two blockers, turns ruleset IDs into the bundle's list IDs with
the loaded blocker's manifest data ("_dynamic" for the person's own rules),
and returns malloc'd JSON for ReArcBufferFree. It keeps nothing. No new
callback: the list changes exactly when the count does, and
ReArcBlockedCountCallback says so.

Checked without a build (the release of 2026-11-19 was building from
out/ReArc-codecs-arm64): action_tracker.cc and rearc_content_blocker.cc
type-check with the tree's clang and plugins from a scratch view of the
tree, against out/ReArc-dev-arm64's generated headers; a control with a
deliberate error fails. The two .mm files change one string each and were
not compiled. engine/tests/check_abi169_imports.py passes against the
patched header (REARC_TEST_ABI_HEADER_DIR). Not built, not run: the shell's
self-test step contentBlockingBlockedListChecks is the run (BL-09).

Touches: chrome/app/framework.exports, chrome/app/framework.order,
chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/{rearc_content_blocker.cc, rearc_engine_abi.h,
rearc_engine_abi.mm, rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm},
extensions/browser/api/declarative_net_request/{action_tracker.cc,
action_tracker.h}.
Applies after tab/097 (the same lines of the export order and the ABI
header).

Bridge 0.79.0, ABI 1.69, feature content_blocking_hosts. No struct changes.

Last rebased: 2026-11-19 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.109 (overlay 17641fac0a).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

